/// Chapter 31 of the guide, written from md-docs/about/performance.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page PerformanceGuide(path: "/docs/guide/performance", title: "Performance", description: "What a build does to be fast, wf build --stats, size budgets, paint timings from wf verify, and the few things that make a site slow.", layout: DocsShell("Performance", kind: .explanation, chapter: t("nav.group.quality"), blurb: "Learn what a build already does to be fast, see what it weighs, set budgets that warn, time pages in a browser, and avoid what makes a site slow.", source: "md-docs/about/performance.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "what-the-build-already-does", label: "What the build already does"), Anchor(id: "see-what-a-build-weighs", label: "See what a build weighs"), Anchor(id: "set-a-size-budget", label: "Set a size budget"), Anchor(id: "time-pages-in-a-browser", label: "Time pages in a browser"), Anchor(id: "avoid-what-makes-a-site-slow", label: "Avoid what makes a site slow")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/security", prevLabel: t("ch.30"), nextTo: "/reference/project", nextLabel: t("ch.32"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This chapter shows you how to keep a WebFluent site fast. Most of the work is already done by the build. Your part is to measure what it writes, set a limit that warns you when it grows, and avoid the few patterns that make a page slow.\n\nIn this chapter:\n\n- What the build already does for you.\n- See what a build weighs, and why each runtime module is in it.\n- Set a size budget, and time each page in a real browser.\n- Avoid the patterns that make a site slow.")

        Heading("What the build already does", id: "what-the-build-already-does").h2

        Markdown("You get these without setting anything:\n\n- **Only the runtime you use.** The *runtime* is the JavaScript the compiled pages call. It is a set of modules, and a build keeps only the ones its code reaches, and of those only the functions its calls reach. A single-page build of one page of static text is an `app.js` of 4.9 kB, 1.9 kB gzipped.\n- **Short names.** A minified build shortens the runtime's own names, its top-level ones and each function's locals. What your pages call keeps its name.\n- **A chunk per page.** `build.split` (on by default) writes each page's code and styles as their own files, loaded the first time its route is shown. A site of one page is one file.\n- **Pre-rendered HTML.** With `build.ssg`, each page's HTML is written at build time, so the first paint needs no script.\n- **One pruned stylesheet.** It holds the rules of only the built-ins you use, and only the design tokens something names.\n- **Precompressed files.** A `.gz` file sits beside every text file, for a host that serves it. `wf serve` sends the same bytes, so Lighthouse run against the dev server measures what a deploy sends.\n- **Images at every width**, with `width` and `height` so nothing shifts, a placeholder while they load, the first image eager and the rest lazy ([Media](/recipes)).\n- **Minified output.** `build.minify` (on by default) strips comments and white space.")

        Heading("See what a build weighs", id: "see-what-a-build-weighs").h2

        Markdown("To see the size of everything a build writes, run the build with `--stats`:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf build --stats")
            ])

        Markdown("This is the output for the project `wf init -t spa` makes, trimmed:")

        CodeBlock(#"  What it weighs
    app.js                               49.5 kB  (16.7 kB gzipped)
    styles.css                           26.5 kB  (5.0 kB gzipped)
    pages/Settings.js                     8.8 kB  (2.2 kB gzipped)
    pages/Profile.js                      5.5 kB  (1.5 kB gzipped)
    pages/Tasks.js                        4.2 kB  (1.3 kB gzipped)
    pages/Home.js                         3.5 kB  (1.1 kB gzipped)
    …
    total                                99.7 kB

  Runtime: 19 of 44 modules, 122.8 kB of 404.6 kB kept, 110.1 kB with its names shortened (before minifying)
    core          26.3 kB  always
    router        13.5 kB  WF.router
    form          12.7 kB  WF.form
    motion        12.6 kB  enter:
    each          10.6 kB  WF.each
    store          9.1 kB  WF.store
    keep           8.9 kB  WF.persist
    field          2.7 kB  WF.field
    …
    left out: keys format offline peer scalars text slot browser host …

  Tokens: 30 nothing in the output names, left out"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("Read it in three parts:\n\n- **What it weighs** lists every text file with its gzipped size. The starter's form brings in `form` and `field`, its store brings in `store` and `keep`, its second page brings in `router`, and its entry animations bring in `motion`.\n- **Runtime** lists each module with what the build kept of it — the functions the program reaches — and what reached it. When a module you did not expect is in the build, look here first.\n- **Tokens** counts the design tokens the build left out because nothing names them.\n\nEach build records its sizes in `.wf-sizes.json` beside the project, so the next `--stats` shows how each file moved since the last build (for example, `+20 B`).\n\nThe project's own scripts are listed by their path under `js/`, such as `js/tilt.js` ([JavaScript interop](/recipes)). The build copies them as written: it does not minify a file it promises to ship byte for byte.")

        Heading("Set a size budget", id: "set-a-size-budget").h2

        Markdown("To be warned when a file grows past a size, name its gzipped limit in `build.budget`:")

        CodeBlock(#"{ "build": { "budget": { "app.js": "40 kB", "styles.css": "30 kB", "pages/Home.js": "10 kB" } } }"#, title: "json")

        Markdown("Any output may have a budget, including a page's chunk and one of your own scripts under `js/`. A build over budget prints a warning and goes on. A CI job that should fail on it can read the same numbers.")

        Heading("Time pages in a browser", id: "time-pages-in-a-browser").h2

        Markdown("To measure how fast each page paints, build the site and run `wf verify` with a budget in milliseconds:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "wf build && wf verify --budget 800")
            ])

        Markdown("`wf verify` loads every route in headless Chrome. For each route it prints the first contentful paint, the number of nodes in the document, and the bytes and requests it took. `--budget 800` fails a route whose first paint is slower than 800 ms. Lighthouse and the browser's performance panel work on the build as on any other site.")

        Heading("Avoid what makes a site slow", id: "avoid-what-makes-a-site-slow").h2

        Markdown("These are the patterns that slow a WebFluent site down, and what to do instead:")

        Table(caption: "Avoid what makes a site slow") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Pattern").header
                    Table.Cell("Why it is slow").header
                    Table.Cell("Do this instead").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A large `data` file") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`data posts = \"posts.json\"` is inlined into the bundle, so a 2 MB file is 2 MB of JavaScript") }
                    Table.Cell("Keep build-time data to what pages show. Fetch the rest, or split it across pages that each read one file")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("A waterfall of fetches")
                    Table.Cell("A resource whose URL depends on another's answer waits for that answer")
                    Table.Cell("Ask for both at once, or have the server send them together")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Layout decided by `viewport`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`viewport` is unknown until the script runs, so the page paints one branch and then swaps it") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Use [responsive values](/docs/guide/styling#responsive-values), which are CSS") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"runtime\": \"full\"`") }
                    Table.Cell("It ships every module")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Use it only when a hand-written script calls `WF` in ways the build cannot see, or an icon's name arrives at run time") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Web fonts")
                    Table.Cell("Each weight is a download")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Use `display=swap` and few weights, or the baseline's system fonts") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("An unkeyed list that changes")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`for item in items` rebuilds the list") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Key it: `for item in items by item.id` moves the nodes that stayed") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Pictures the build cannot process")
                    Table.Cell("An SVG, a URL or a path built at run time is used as written: one size, no placeholder")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Use a literal `src:` into `public/`, or declare the picture with `image` ([Media](/recipes))") }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
